---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | SheetPilot AI" description="Privacy Policy and data practices for SheetPilot AI.">
  <div className="min-h-screen bg-canvas-soft text-ink font-sans relative py-16 px-4 md:px-8">
    <div className="mesh-gradient-bg" />
    
    <div className="max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-canvas border border-hairline rounded-xl shadow-xl p-8 md:p-12 relative z-10 space-y-8">
      
      {/* Header */}
      <div className="border-b border-hairline pb-6">
        <h1 className="display-sm font-semibold text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p className="text-xs text-mute mt-2">Last updated: June 12, 2026</p>
      </div>

      {/* Intro */}
      <div className="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed space-y-4">
        <p>
          At SheetPilot AI, we are committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring a secure experience while utilizing our natural language spreadsheet assistant. This Privacy Policy details how we handle, protect, and process user data, specifically regarding Google OAuth APIs and spreadsheet synchronization.
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* Sections */}
      <div className="space-y-6">
        
        <section className="space-y-3">
          <h2 className="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">1. Data We Access and Collect</h2>
          <div className="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed space-y-2">
            <p>
              When you sign in using your Google Account, we request specific scopes to allow the application to function. We access the following information:
            </p>
            <ul className="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
              <li><strong>Basic Profile Information:</strong> Your email address, full name, and profile picture, which are used solely to create and identify your account.</li>
              <li><strong>Google Sheets Files:</strong> Through the requested <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets</code> scope, the app accesses the specific spreadsheet sheets you sync or open in order to execute your plain English cleanup/formatting commands.</li>
              <li><strong>Google Drive Files:</strong> Through the <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly</code> scope, we list available spreadsheets to let you easily import files from your Google Drive into the workspace.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section className="space-y-3">
          <h2 className="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">2. How We Use Your Data</h2>
          <div className="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed space-y-2">
            <p>
              We only use the data retrieved from Google APIs to perform the operations you explicitly direct.
            </p>
            <ul className="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
              <li>We perform spreadsheet transformations (deleting rows, formatting columns, generating formulas, compiling charts) strictly at your command.</li>
              <li>Spreadsheet data is processed and displayed inside your browser session.</li>
              <li>Your Google OAuth credentials (refresh tokens) are securely encrypted and stored on our database cluster (MongoDB Atlas) to maintain your connection, and are never shared with third parties.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section className="space-y-3">
          <h2 className="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">3. Data Retention and Safety</h2>
          <div className="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed space-y-2">
            <p>
              We prioritize data safety and do not retain copies of your spreadsheet data on our servers longer than necessary to run your requested AI operations.
            </p>
            <ul className="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
              <li>All API interactions between the frontend, our backend server, and the Google API servers are fully encrypted using Transport Layer Security (TLS/SSL).</li>
              <li>We do not sell, trade, or rent any of your spreadsheet or profile data.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section className="space-y-3">
          <h2 className="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">4. Google API Services User Data Policy Compliance</h2>
          <div className="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              SheetPilot AI's use of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" className="text-link underline hover:text-ink">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section className="space-y-3">
          <h2 className="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">5. Contact Us</h2>
          <div className="text-xs text-body leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or wish to request the deletion of your account and linked OAuth tokens, please contact us at:
            </p>
            <p className="mt-2 font-semibold text-ink">
              Email: salikazeem123@gmail.com
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>

      {/* Button to go back */}
      <div className="border-t border-hairline pt-6 flex justify-between items-center">
        <a href="/" className="btn-secondary text-xs inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 transition-all">
          &larr; Back to Landing Page
        </a>
        <a href="/auth/login" className="btn-primary text-xs inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 transition-all shadow">
          Go to Sign In &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
